cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below. CINA is a
  graduate research project (preliminary methodology pilot). No DOI is assigned;
  use the GitHub URL.
title: "CINA: Climate Issue-Network Analysis Framework"
abstract: >-
  CINA is an end-to-end LLM → graph → LLM pipeline for climate negotiation
  intelligence. A single LLM extraction step produces stance scores with
  Bayesian credible intervals, NATO 4-axis policy instruments (Hood 1983;
  Howlett 2019; Capano et al. 2025), 5-frame typology (Snow & Benford 1988),
  and procedural-authority signals (Tallberg 2010). Downstream, a heterogeneous
  Country × Issue × Group graph is analysed with Leiden community detection
  (Traag et al. 2019) and a multi-task heterogeneous R-GAT (PyTorch). Briefing
  generation operates under a graph-grounded discipline that requires every
  output claim to cite both a verbatim evidence quote and a structural fact.
  The framework is piloted retrospectively on the COP30 Belém Adaptation
  Indicators outcome (FCCC/PA/CMA/2025/L.25E, November 2025).
